+    same directory can be written by another process while this walk runs.  Each
+    child is therefore resolved to its object, opened without following links,
+    and compared through the descriptor with the object that was resolved a
+    moment earlier.  The removal itself goes through ``_unlink_verified``, which
+    moves the verified object to a fresh name first, so a swap of the child's
+    name cannot redirect the deletion or the recursion.
